ad":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.3281820342869952,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":0.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.10179127420376011,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":75.9,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07488604578219761,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":94.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.007627153669129916,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":40.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.02166966700315805,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":63.9,"_gate_insider_own":0.04004,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":26.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Walker & Dunlop, Inc., through its subsidiaries, originates, sells, and services a range of multifamily and other commercial real estate financing products and services for owners and developers of real estate in the United States. The company operates through three segments: Capital Markets, Servicing & Asset Management, and Corporate. The company offers first mortgage, second trust, supplemental, construction, mezzanine, preferred equity, and small-balance loans. It also provides finance for multifamily, manufactured housing communities, student housing, affordable housing, small balance loans, and senior housing properties under the Fannie Mae's Delegated Underwriting and Servicing program and Freddie Mac; and construction and permanent loans to developers and owners of multifamily housing, affordable housing, senior housing, and healthcare facilities. In addition, the company acts as a debt broker to work with life insurance companies, banks, and other institutional investors to find debt and/or equity solution for the borrowers' needs; and offers property sales brokerage services to owners and developers of multifamily properties, and commercial real estate and multifamily property appraisals for various investors. Further, it provides multifamily appraisal and valuation services; and real estate-related investment banking and advisory services, including housing market research. Additionally, the company offers servicing and asset-managing the portfolio of loans; originates loans through its principal lending and investing activities; and manages third-party capital invested in tax credit equity funds focused on the LIHTC sector and other commercial real estate sectors. Walker & Dunlop, Inc. was founded in 1937 and is headquartered in Bethesda, Maryland.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William Mallory Walker | Chairman, President & CEO | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $842K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 16%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $18K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Walker & Dunlop, Inc is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.4B market cap on $1.2B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $680M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +14.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.2\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.5% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.0% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +14.2% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.9) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 241% leaves essentially no coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 23% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"We Wouldn't Be Too Quick To Buy Walker & Dunlop, Inc. (NYSE:WD) Before It Goes Ex-Dividend","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/diversified-financials/nyse-wd/walker-dunlop/news/we-wouldnt-be-too-quick-to-buy-walker-dunlop-inc-nysewd-befo","date":"2026-11-15","timestamp":1794747418.97,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.361,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a","dividend"]},{"title":"How Walker & Dunlop Inc (WD) Affects Rotational Strategy Timing","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/78/How_Walker_Dunlop_Inc_WD_Affects_Rotational_Strategy_Timing_111426080602_1794661562.html","date":"2026-11-14","timestamp":1794661562.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Walker & Dunlop Inc's Dividend Analysis","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/walker-dunlop-incs-dividend-analysis-101408855.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795169648.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.718,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Walker & Dunlop Arranges $270 Million Refinancing for Nasser Freres\u2019 The Greyson in Jersey City","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/walker-dunlop-arranges-270-million-010000306.html","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795050000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"AllianceBernstein Reports 5.7% Ownership Stake in Walker & Dunlop as of September 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/alliancebernstein-reports-57-ownership-stake-in-walker-dunlop-as-of-september-2026","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794856370.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"co